{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","text":"BatchLimit"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The 100 events are what TelemetryDeck’s SwiftSDK sends in a request. The 333,333 bytes of an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event are a third of Ingest API v3’s limit: TelemetryDeck refuses a whole request when one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event’s JSON is over 1,000,000 bytes as its server writes it, which may be larger than the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder’s, and a third leaves room for the escapes a re-encoder commonly adds, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\u"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and four hex digits for a character outside ASCII, and a space after each "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":":"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":","},{"type":"text","text":". A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"larger event is left out as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck documents no limit on a request; its 1,000,000 bytes are the encoder’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bound, the most one event may be, which keeps a request to a size a retry can send again."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"TelemetryDeck’s limits on one request: 100 events and 1,000,000 bytes of body, and 333,333","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bytes of one event.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:21TelemetryDeckEncoding0aB12BatchEncoderV10batchLimit12PropertyJSON0dG0VvpZ","title":"batchLimit","modules":[{"name":"TelemetryDeckEncoding"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit"}],"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property","roleHeading":"Type Property","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift#L134","fileName":"TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder.swift"}},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding","doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/telemetrydeckencoding\/telemetrydeckbatchencoder\/batchlimit"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/documentation\/TelemetryDeckEncoding\/TelemetryDeckBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://PropertyJSON/documentation/PropertyJSON/BatchLimit":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/propertyjson\/batchlimit","identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","type":"topic","title":"BatchLimit","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchLimit","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The most an ingestion endpoint takes in one request: how